---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import MetronomePanel from '../../components/MetronomePanel.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Free Online Piano Metronome – BPM, Tap Tempo & Time Signature" description="Free browser piano metronome with accurate Web Audio timing, 40–200 BPM, tap tempo, 2/4, 3/4 and 4/4 accents. No app, signup or API needed." canonicalPath="/tools/metronome/" crumbs={[{name:'Metronome',href:'/tools/metronome/'}]}>
<section class="container page-hero tool-hero"><span class="eyebrow">STEADY RHYTHM · BETTER PRACTICE</span><h1>Find your tempo.<br/><em>Keep your time.</em></h1><p class="lead">Use the browser metronome while practising scales and chords. Tap a comfortable beat, select 2/4, 3/4 or 4/4, and speed up gradually as your timing improves.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/tools/virtual-piano/">Play alongside the 88-key piano ↗</a><a class="btn" href="/tools/chord-progressions/">Try chord progressions</a></div></section>
<section class="container section-compact"><MetronomePanel /></section>
<section class="container section"><div class="learning-grid"><div class="learning-panel"><h2>How to practise with a metronome</h2><p>Set a slow tempo of 60–80 BPM and play one note per click. Each click corresponds to a quarter note, including in 2/4, 3/4 and 4/4. When the notes feel comfortable, increase the tempo by five BPM.</p><p>The first beat of each measure sounds higher and is highlighted in the visual counter. Tap Tempo calculates a BPM estimate from your recent taps.</p></div><div class="learning-panel"><h2>Timing and privacy</h2><p>Clicks are scheduled in Web Audio a little ahead of time for more consistent timing than JavaScript timers alone. If you switch away from the tab, the metronome stops to avoid stale or unexpected playback.</p><p>The metronome is also embedded on the <a href="/tools/virtual-piano/">Virtual Piano</a> page, so you can practise with both tools visible. No microphone, cookies, uploads or database are required.</p></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
